  "note": "A1+ Unit 1 Lesson 1.3 rebuilt on 2026-11-10 under the A1+ lesson standards approved 2026-10-27 and the user's 2026-11-09 rule that every A1+ lesson follows up the A1 lesson with the same number. A1 1.3 Two People: They and Are joins two people with and and says what they are doing (They are swimming.); A1+ 1.3 says what two people do, with they/we and no -s, against he/she with -s: Sofia and Luis swim in the morning, Ana swims in the morning, Sofia and Luis run in the park, Diego runs in the park. Learn uses the approved contrast pairs (D2). Swim is new (A1 has only swimming); run is A1 4.8. No days and no 'every day' (on + day would be a second new relationship; frequency comes in 1.6-1.7). Listen contrasts no -s, -s and A1 1.3's are/is ...-ing by ear (swim cards by subject only, because They swim in the morning. has no natural -ing partner). In the morning is A1 4.5. A pair photo also shows one woman or one man doing the action, so it is never a wrong picture for a he/she sentence. The previous 1.3 (Which time actually works?: from/to, before/after) returns with A1+ 4.10 and 5.7.",
